From fe471ebe157627d0b6b411c279166e2851a99d71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:13:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 41/52] Don't cancel every in-band command when a completion is
 aborted

Aborting a stale completion, autosuggestion or decoration future already
cancels its own commands (on_cancel / kill on drop). The extra session-wide
cancel_active_commands() also dropped unrelated queued commands, which on an
in-band session (the web build, SSH) are all of them. Also re-parse the input
once external commands have loaded instead of reusing the cached parse.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 app/src/terminal/input.rs             | 24 ++++--------------------
 app/src/terminal/input/decorations.rs | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 app/src/terminal/view.rs              |  8 +-------
 3 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

